      particularly disagreeable tabby of your acquaintance are all included.

   b. "Harm, distress or fear" means what a reasonable cat would consider harm,
      distress or fear. The cat is the authority on this, not you.

   c. The following do not breach this condition: veterinary care, however
      poorly received; the administration of medicine; transport in a carrier;
      the closing of a door the cat wished to remain open; and the withholding
      of food at hours the cat considers appropriate but the clock does not.

   d. Being ignored is not distress. It is a negotiating position.

